=== LRC14 gap/automaton carrier scout S173 ===
Status: synthesis computation and quotient guardrail; not a proof

External source notes
  arXiv:2506.04110: 2-adic Littlewood work uses doubling of continued-fraction data as a live obstruction carrier; for this pass it contributes the retained field 'doubling transition state'.
  Ostrowski-Hadamard gap theorem: lacunary exponent support with ratio bounded above 1 creates natural-boundary behavior; for LRC it is a boundary warning, not a scalar certificate.
  DOI 10.5555/1109557.1109610: the ACM record resolves to a computational-geometry 'large sticks and potatoes' paper, not Fermat-Catalan; here it contributes only a visibility/inscribed-core analogy.
  Fermat-Catalan: the useful abstraction is the hyperbolic exponent budget 1/p + 1/q + 1/r < 1 as a finite-exception ledger.

Finite automata
  fibbinary_no_adjacent_one: states=['last0', 'last1', 'dead'], start=last0, accept=['last0', 'last1']
    interpretation: binary normal forms with no adjacent 1s; doubling appends 0
  moser_base4_01_digit_language: states=['ok', 'dead'], start=ok, accept=['ok']
    interpretation: sums of distinct powers of 4; multiply by 4 appends 0

